 Maintainers ## Context Styling in...\n3. [KI] **KI: Rich Core (Console, Alignment & Core Layouts)** (`.ki-base/knowledge/KI_rich_align.md`, score: 14.574)\n   > ...pipeline of Rich: houses the primary `Console` class, ANSI escape sequence decoder, cell width calculators, border box constants, and alignment/column containers. It coordinates measurement, rendering, and...\n4. [KI] **KI: Rich Core (Segments, Styles & Atomic Primitives)** (`.ki-base/knowledge/KI_rich_region.md`, score: 12.85)\n   > ...last_verified: 2026-11-08 --> # KI: Rich Core (Segments, Styles & Atomic Primitives) ## Overview Defines the atomic rendering primitives of Rich: `Segment` (minimal text+style tuple), `Style` (ANSI attributes...\n5. [KI] **KI: Rich Core (Layouts, Highlighters & Logging)** (`.ki-base/knowledge/KI_rich_default.md`, score: 5.671)\n   > .../ `ReprHighlighter`: Base classes applying style spans via regular expression matching. ## Key Components | Class / Function | File | Purpose | |---|---|---| | `Layout` | `rich/layout.py` |...\n\n*Showing 5 of 13 results. Call `ki_search(query='Style double underline ANSI markup HTML SVG export style composition', page=2)` (or `offset=5`) to view more.*"}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_search"},"isError":false,"durationMs":64,"timestamp":1794169789596},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_Y8Y932TrKGnhl9uvj0HQ3NJz","toolName":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_instructions","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Global AI Instructions for ki-manager\n\n## 1. Project Navigation & Architecture\n`.ki-base` (knowledge_root) is the **system container** for the entire knowledge infrastructure (analogous to `.git/` in Git).\n\n```\n<project_root>/\n├── .ki-base/                 ← SYSTEM CONTAINER (do not pollute with .ki.md)\n│   ├── config.json             ← Machine-specific environment config (venv path, etc.)\n│   ├── ki_config.json          ← Project knowledge configuration\n│   ├── doc_config.json         ← Manifest of tracked modules and Knowledge Items\n│   ├── DIR_INDEX.md            ← Auto-generated project directory tree\n│   ├── coverage_matrix.md      ← Audit report (from audit_coverage)\n│   ├── knowledge/              ← STRICTLY ALL Knowledge Items (*.ki.md) live HERE!\n│   │   ├── _OVERVIEW.ki.md     ← Project overview stub (MUST NOT be deleted)\n│   │   └── <module>.ki.md      ← Module Knowledge Items\n│   └── decisions/              ← Architectural Decision Records (*.md ADRs)\n├── AGENTS.md                   ← Project instructions for AI agents in harness\n└── CLAUDE.md                   ← Instructions for Claude Code / Anthropic\n```\n\n- **`DIR_INDEX.md`** (`.ki-base/DIR_INDEX.md`) — project directory tree.\n- **`doc_config.json`** (`.ki-base/doc_config.json`) — manifest of tracked artifacts.\n- **`_OVERVIEW.ki.md`** (`.ki-base/knowledge/_OVERVIEW.ki.md`) — start here for high-level architecture.\n- **Harness & Agent Instructions Guide**: see `ki://agent-rules.md` or `ki_instructions(document=\"agent-rules\")` for recommended snippets for `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md`.\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> 1. NEVER place `*.ki.md` files directly in the root of `.ki-base/`. All Knowledge Items must reside in `.ki-base/knowledge/`.\n> 2. NEVER delete `.ki-base/knowledge/`. The initial `_OVERVIEW.ki.md` (~640 bytes) is a bootstrap stub, not a duplicate. Deleting `knowledge/` breaks audit, scaffolding, and dependency analysis.\n\n## 2. Forced Efficiency (Anti-Hallucinations)\n1. **Mandatory Planning Template**:\n   Before making code changes, your initial plan (Implementation Plan) **MUST** include:\n   - **Affected layers**: [which subsystems are affected]\n   - **Read KIs**: [LIST of files from `.ki-base/knowledge/` which you read for this task]. *If the list is empty — read KIs before writing code!*\n   - **KIs Constraints**: [which approaches are prohibited by current architecture]\n\n2. **Strict Adherence**:\n   - Always read relevant KIs before modifying a module.\n- Use `ki_list()` to view all documented items, `ki_search(query=\"...\")` to find topics, and `ki_read(rel_path=\"...\")` to read documentation.\n   - For read-only analysis tools (`audit_coverage`, `generate_dir_index`, `ki_scaffold_status`, `git_diff_secured`), call `ki_call(tool=\"...\")`.\n   - For state-modifying operations (`git_checkpoint`, `write_know_file`, `edit_know_file`, `ki_scaffold`, `create_adr`), call `ki_mutate(tool=\"...\", args={...})`.\n   - To inspect schemas of available tools, call `ki_tools(name=\"<tool_name>\")`.\n   \n## 3. Workflow-driven Execution\n1. Check `ki://workflows/` resources or MCP Prompts if the user asks for a complex documentation task.\n2. These workflows are your \"operating system\". You **MUST** follow their steps exactly as written.\n"}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_instructions"},"isError":false,"durationMs":66,"timestamp":1794169789599},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.encrypted\",\"data\":\"gAAAAABq8Nu-9hUnoc-xu2t8lmlsTCWDYUzXGaFczV4jnl5upq2ee4l1uSfRGOZLUSGnQc8y3bzoZ70Sf0EIfepq1EnTi1oD83JgItJw-QqvElbIRRtMLXvGV2qpPaznCeI_0IRxqFiy4OrKTDrRlskS1PWew2txdPO9jytSmQL5-Vx5mztM6yHSP22j1_yIHq55FkgMelaQbsP1WN0EWSJnj03l2c1iP4wGsggQatIQ0320vA8tTYX7MSAHjhUP-YmmHEynM6Sg93OBzDNnKnzwTnYtAzt1ldYSlgmT_h3yhRp0knQtGW7lyQ5ajlFap4EmowGuDHOAB8g9Wx_zLGQZWUOK2DscTX_yRdTs07dtp6j0gvsU_b3cgBu0K_l84NR9VZ8bZz8JOV8oUJvojJOllCOC5Jq51I6jeeDpTTVFy33PX3dUMZ5T0odsXLAhu8Jm1rwfrzqx-SuK4SIHy0n-g8Sg7qSfz8Ib1_sbs6c_9vmaL6Jt0zUyGQFrh6wB-Jw6Jydf_kijWFk9DVJCEo71pmO6Ry4HjdWRyeF2WzLfTuQsUhnSBjIAfN7zTBcjfxtzbGBE24XBDNOvQQxMndsElXBSxVr0JWzYLywLzXsOD2R9_eO_BXYL8apsqZSJ1bg7RDRbFpBUaLnhoexnsruwowWpAP42h5K2tIa8WV_WZg-XpBi6IQC8Q-GYSI8c1rMye8VphVzjo_aG7zgZ4pHO9XI4Jq1Ba4YypnwrC14kETJ62Z2riloVMUgEgBq6tJk0eQYPuqvqiRgaE8HQOHdUl_uqYb3XzeQC0p4mxQHfToPWr4rxY3NVRGfuOcohstT61no8-HSUgP5Jo3R33iasn89_YApCFDKrYMFX6tA4remcC7p5-ZShU1YYs0aWLFgDFBU-HTk3_Ion4KHwiiqnlLzIkDitiE2ZaCfljqwjzaaqI_yUV35F3lGPwlsmgj34Bz1PU0Hq_fc0RPPXa0XV9_lAne-8sOitsG